  competitorsIntro: 'Oman is the cheapest GCC country for international schooling per 2026 industry reports — Muscat premium fees regularly reach OMR 6,200-10,000+/year (~USD 16,120-26,000+/year), meaningfully below Dubai equivalents where premium schools regularly exceed AED 90,000 (~OMR 9,400+). Fee tiers span budget (OMR 1,800-3,200/year primary), mid-tier (OMR 3,800-5,800/year primary), and premium (OMR 6,200-9,500+/year primary, OMR 7,500-10,000+/year secondary/IBDP). British School Muscat (BSM, since 1971), Cheltenham Muscat (2021 UK franchise), Downe House Muscat (2022 girls-only), TAISM (American, US Embassy sponsored), and ABA Oman International School anchor the premium tier. Sohar has ABIS (IB continuum), Salalah has British School Salalah (BSM southern campus). Cambridge is the dominant exam board.',
