  // ── FAQs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  faqs: [
    { q: 'Where does Smartious sit relative to Oman\'s premium international schools like BSM, Cheltenham Muscat, TAISM, and ABA?',       a: 'Oman\'s premium tier — British School Muscat (BSM, OMR 3,700-8,950/year, since 1971, dual A-Level/IB, 6-12 month waiting list), Cheltenham Muscat (Al Bandar UK franchise since 2021), Downe House Muscat (girls-only since 2022), TAISM (US Embassy sponsored, only such school in Oman, OMR 4,990-9,710/year), ABA Oman International School (Madinat Qaboos, US curriculum), Sultan\'s School (bilingual British + IB, Sultan Qaboos founder) — provides physical campus premium British, IB, or American curriculum. Smartious provides live online Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD at USD 2,160-6,480/year (~OMR 830-2,495/year) with identical qualifications, immediate enrolment (no 6-12 month waiting list), small class sizes, and 1-hour GST offset from EAT teaching. Fee arbitrage substantial; qualifications and university acceptance identical.' },
    { q: 'BSM and ABA have 6-12 month waiting lists. Can Smartious bridge us or serve as alternative?',                                   a: 'Both scenarios common in Oman. As waiting-list bridge: Smartious carries your child through Cambridge IGCSE or A-Level for 6-12 months until BSM or ABA place opens, with credit-forward on transfer to physical school. As permanent alternative: same Cambridge / IB / American qualifications delivered live online at USD 2,160-6,480/year vs OMR 3,700-8,950+/year, with immediate enrolment and no waiting.' },
    { q: 'Where do Omani students sit Cambridge examinations?',                                                                            a: 'British Council Muscat is Oman\'s primary Cambridge IGCSE and A-Level examination centre. Board exam fees run approximately OMR 500-1,500+ per session. Some Oman international schools (BSM, SIS Sohar, ABQ Seeb, and others) may accept external candidates. Salalah, Sohar, Nizwa, and Sur families travel to Muscat for examinations (drive or short domestic flight).' },
    { q: 'Is homeschooling legal in Oman?',                                                                                                a: 'Oman\'s Ministry of Education (MoE) regulates the education framework and issues equivalency certificates for IB Diploma, IGCSE/A-Level, and Omani General Education Diploma. Substantial expatriate community operates under residence permit frameworks and pursues international curriculum via authorised international schools or online providers. Most Smartious Oman delivery is in the secondary (Cambridge IGCSE Years 10-11, A-Level Years 12-13, IB Diploma) window — legally straightforward for all Omani and expat families.' },
    { q: 'How does live class scheduling work given GST and Nairobi teaching hours?',                                                     a: 'Gulf Standard Time (GST UTC+4) is one hour ahead of East Africa Time (EAT UTC+3). Smartious live classes 9 AM – 12 PM Nairobi teaching = 10 AM – 1 PM local Muscat time — natural school-day window matching Muscat school hours. Afternoon 3 PM – 6 PM GST slot also available. Recorded sessions 24/7.' },
    { q: 'What Omani universities accept Cambridge, IB, and AP qualifications?',                                                          a: 'Sultan Qaboos University (public, main national), German University of Technology in Oman (GUtech, Muscat), Muscat University (Aston University UK partnership), University of Nizwa, Dhofar University (Salalah), Sohar University, Modern College of Business and Science (MCBS), Middle East College Muscat. Oman MoE equivalency system authenticates foreign qualifications for university admission and employment.' },
    { q: 'How does Smartious solve the Sohar, Salalah, Nizwa, or Sur international school gap?',                                          a: 'Oman outside Muscat has significantly fewer international schools — Sohar has fewer than 5 (ABIS, SIS Sohar, Pakistan School), Salalah has British School Salalah plus a small local band, Nizwa has essentially no international curriculum options, Sur has very limited options. Families historically face Muscat relocation, boarding, or overseas study. Smartious delivers Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD directly to all Oman regions — no relocation, no boarding, full curriculum choice.' },
    { q: 'Can my Omani child combine Omani national school with Smartious for Cambridge?',                                                a: 'Yes — a common Omani family configuration. Omani national curriculum in the morning for Omani General Education Diploma and Sultan Qaboos University pathway continuity, Smartious Cambridge / IB / AP in the afternoon (3 PM – 6 PM GST window). Family combines Omani national qualifications with international qualifications for maximum university options.' },
    { q: 'What Oman regions does Smartious serve?',                                                                                        a: 'Muscat (MSQ — BSM/ABA area, Al Khuwair, Al Bandar — Cheltenham/Downe House area, Al Ghubra — Indian School Muscat area, Bawshar, Ruwi, Qurum), Seeb (Sultan\'s School, RGSG Muscat, Downe House Muscat, KGIS, Al Hail South, Mabela, Knowledge Oasis Muscat), Sohar (Al Batinah North industrial and port — ABIS, SIS Sohar), Salalah (Dhofar southern coast — British School Salalah), Nizwa (Ad Dakhiliyah interior cultural capital), and Sur (Ash Sharqiyah North eastern coastal — Oman LNG). Also broader Oman via live online delivery.' },
    { q: 'What internet speed does Smartious require in Oman?',                                                                           a: 'Sustained ~5-10 Mbps per student for live HD video conferencing. Omantel Fiber, Ooredoo Oman Fiber, and Awasr Fiber residential broadband across Muscat, Seeb, Sohar, Salalah, Nizwa, and Sur routinely deliver 100+ Mbps. 5G mobile widely available in Muscat and expanding to other cities.' },
  ],

